    "title": "How to live stream Michigan vs Arizona: NCAA Final Four, time, TV channel",
    "text": "The second game of the 2026 NCAA Tournament Final Four features a marquee showdown between the Arizona Wildcats and the Michigan Wolverines, both teams chasing a ticket to the national championship.Tip-off is set for 8:49 p.m. ET on Saturday night at Lucas Oil Stadium, with coverage airing live on TBS and streaming across DIRECTV.AdvertisementMORE: 8 most entertaining players to watch in the 2026 Final FourWhen: Saturday, April 4, 2026Time: 8:49 PM ETTV Channel: TBS, TNT, truTVMichigan enters as one of the hottest teams left in the field, building momentum with back-to-back strong performances in the Sweet 16 and Elite Eight. The Wolverines have relied on disciplined defense and timely scoring, limiting opponents and capitalizing in key moments late in games.Their ability to control tempo and dictate the style of play has been a major factor in their tournament success.Meanwhile, Arizona has looked like one of the most complete teams in March Madness, advancing through a challenging region with consistent play on both ends of the floor. The Wildcats punched their ticket to the Final Four with an impressive Elite Eight performance, controlling the game with balanced scoring, strong rebounding, and efficient offense.AdvertisementTheir ability to push the pace while also executing in half-court sets has made them difficult to defend throughout the tournament. Watch Michigan vs Arizona Final Four Live on DIRECTV Regional restrictions may apply. If you purchase a product or register for an account through one of the links on our site, we may receive compensation.",
